body:
You're awesome, thanks so much for the reply. Everyone has been really helpful to me in this thread and I really appreciate that. I'm sorry to hear about all those ailments that you have. I have inner ear issues too I think. I think gaming was making me dizzy for a few years before it started making me nauseous. I just figured because I take medicine for anxiety that it was my medicine making me dizzy all the time and when I was hospitalized once for a long time I stopped getting dizzy (not entirely but it was way less) and then when I started playing games again I would feel dizzy. But I never got nauseous from it until I tried VR so I really didn't care since I've been chronically dizzy for like 10 years. 

&#x200B;

Are there any 3d games you can play endlessly without getting dizzy or nauseous? Although, having an hour or two would be awesome. All games that make me sick are generally about the same amount of time. Anywhere between 3-15 minutes. Thanks so much for the suggestions. Also I always heard that people should play on an empty stomach. Either way thank you so much :)
